      "content": "\"infestation\" is a strong word for it, but yeah, that's exactly how it feels. like they're just small, pesky things that don't belong, but they're everywhere. it's so distracting. \n\nsince you mentioned they're like a metaphor for a poorly managed collection, is there a way to actually deal with them? i don't want to just keep finding these little disruptions every time i open a new folder. how do i clean out the \"noise\" so i can actually focus on the important manuscripts?",
